infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title One connection vs six: what HTTP/2 trades away
  desc Multiplexing kills HTTP-layer HoL but folds six failure domains into one
  compares
    - label HTTP/1.1 — up to 6 connections per origin
      children
        - label Up to 6 TCP connections
          desc Browser opens ~6 sockets per origin to get parallelism
        - label One request at a time per connection
          desc Serial pipelining; a slow response HoL-blocks its own queue
        - label 6 independent failure domains
          desc A lost packet freezes 1 connection; the other 5 keep flowing
        - label 6x connection setup
          desc TCP + TLS handshake on each of the six sockets
    - label HTTP/2 — one connection per origin
      children
        - label 1 TCP connection
          desc All streams share one socket, multiplexed by stream ID
        - label Many streams at once
          desc Interleaved binary frames; no HTTP-layer HoL
        - label 1 shared failure domain
          desc A lost segment stalls every stream via TCP in-order delivery
        - label 1x connection setup
          desc One TCP + TLS handshake, ALPN negotiated once
theme
  palette #f59e0b #6366f1
